cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Reproducible pipeline for analyzing intraplate heat-flow anomalies relative to tectonic boundaries"
message: "If you use this repository, please cite it as follows."
type: software

doi: 10.5281/zenodo.19493652
version: "2.0"

authors:
  - family-names: Gaujac
    given-names: Cristiano
    affiliation: "Independent Researcher"
    email: papers.gaujac@gmail.com

abstract: >
  This repository provides a fully reproducible computational pipeline
  designed to investigate the spatial relationship between global
  terrestrial heat-flow measurements and tectonic structures.
  
  The pipeline enables systematic evaluation of heat-flow behavior
  as a function of distance from tectonic boundaries, incorporating
  multiple statistical controls, clustering analyses, and robustness
  tests.
  
  Results generated using this framework demonstrate that statistically
  significant intraplate heat-flow anomalies persist far beyond
  classical tectonic domains, challenging models in which tectonic
  proximity is assumed to be the dominant control on heat flow.
  
  All analyses, figures, and derived results are fully reproducible
  using the provided code and documented data sources.

keywords:
  - geophysics
  - heat flow
  - tectonic boundaries
  - intraplate processes
  - geospatial analysis
  - geothermal anomalies
  - reproducible pipeline
  - scientific reproducibility

